# Normalise line endings to LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default) rewrites files as
# CRLF whenever git materialises them on checkout, while Prettier's default
# `endOfLine: "lf"` rejects CRLF. Which files are affected depends on which ones
# git happened to touch last, so `pnpm format:check` — and therefore
# `pnpm check` — passes or fails based on your recent branch switches rather
# than on the content. This pins it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
